      "content": "Besides regular NPK levels, healthy soil biology includes a diverse community of bacteria, fungi, and other microorganisms that aid in nutrient breakdown, uptake, and disease suppression. A well-aerated soil with proper moisture and diverse organic content encourages this life. Signs of a healthy soil microbiome include earthworm activity, healthy root growth, and knowing that your plants are disease-free. Consider conducting a soil biology test or incorporating biochar or compost tea to enhance microbial activity.",
